+Client Tool presentation plugin. `ui-conversation` dispatches streamed `tool-activity` and ordered formal `tool-call` Conversation Nodes through their matching keys of `conversation.chat.node`; this package renders pending rows plus each formal root and Code Dispatch child, then dispatches every atomic formal call through the keyed `tool.call.toolview` slot. Unregistered Tool names use the generic card.
 
 Business UI packages register only their wire Tool names and atomic views. They do not pair Session events, rebuild the transcript, or own root/subcall topology. The Runtime remains authoritative for call/result pairing, lifecycle, and recursive `subCalls` projection; the conversation view remains authoritative for ChatFlow placement.
 
 ## Rendering contract
 
-`ToolCallTree` receives one root `ToolCallBlock` that already contains recursive `subCalls`, selection state, the session `cwd`, and Host callbacks for opening files and inspecting calls. It recursively walks the standard call blocks and sends the root and children at every depth through the same atomic dispatch path, without subscribing to a separate parent-to-children map.
+`ToolActivityView` receives name-only pending calls from the first streamed Tool delta and renders ordinary non-expandable rows without parsing or displaying partial arguments. `ToolCallTree` receives one root `ToolCallBlock` that already contains recursive `subCalls`, selection state, the first streamed start time, the session `cwd`, and Host callbacks for opening files and inspecting calls. It recursively walks the standard call blocks and sends the root and children at every depth through the same atomic dispatch path, without subscribing to a separate parent-to-children map.
+
+Every pending or running row shows a quiet gray elapsed timer followed by gray `ing`, and the whole row carries the same scanning glare as a running Think row. Formal settlement freezes the timer, stops the glare, and removes persistent status copy; hovering or focusing the settled row reveals gray `Done` in the reserved status position. Reduced-motion preferences disable the glare.
 
